parameters.jsCode:
// Keep only reviews still waiting for a reply: Status reads "Needs reply"
// (any capitalisation) AND the Review Text is non-empty. The CONFIG fields
// ride along on every item because the CONFIG Set node merged them in.
// If nothing matches, this returns zero items and the workflow quietly
// stops — no AI calls, no drafts, no digest email, no noise.
return $input.all().filter(item => {
  const j = item.json;
  const status = String(j['Status'] || '').trim().toLowerCase();
  const text = String(j['Review Text'] || '').trim();
  return status === 'needs reply' && text.length > 0;
});

parameters.message:
The Review Reply Assistant tried to draft a reply but the AI step failed, so this review has no draft yet.

Reviewer: {{ $json.Reviewer }}
Stars: {{ $json.Stars }}
Review: {{ $json['Review Text'] }}

Error: {{ $json.error.message }}

Nothing is lost: the review still says "Needs reply" in the Reviews tab, so it will be picked up again on the next run once the cause is fixed. Common causes: an expired or out-of-credit OpenAI API key.

parameters.jsCode:
// Pair each AI response with its review (the items come back in the same
// order they went in) and pull draft_reply out of the JSON safely.
// If the AI output cannot be parsed, draft_reply stays empty and
// parse_failed = "YES" — the Save step then marks that row
// "write by hand" and the digest email counts it, so a bad draft can
// never kill the run or slip through looking finished.
const reviews = $('Keep Reviews Needing Replies').all();
return $input.all().map((item, i) => {
  const review = (reviews[i] && reviews[i].json) || {};
  let draft = '';
  let failed = '';
  try {
    const raw = item.json.choices[0].message.content;
    draft = String(JSON.parse(raw).draft_reply || '').trim();
    if (!draft) failed = 'YES';
  } catch (e) {
    failed = 'YES';
  }
  return { json: {
    reviewer: review['Reviewer'] || '',
    stars: review['Stars'] || '',
    review_text: review['Review Text'] || '',
    draft_reply: draft,
    parse_failed: failed,
    status: 'Awaiting approval'
  }};
});
